# Commented documentation placeholders only. No secrets belong in source.
# Set these in the SERVER process environment after account approval.
# Both are required; partial configuration never calls inference.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=YOUR_APPROVED_ACCOUNT_ID_LATER
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=YOUR_WORKERS_AI_TOKEN_LATER
# .env files are not automatically loaded. Do not use VITE_ prefixed secrets.
# PayPal Sandbox only. Both are required; partial configuration never calls PayPal.
# The adapter only talks to https://api-m.sandbox.paypal.com and refuses FIXTURE-CAP- ids.
# PAYPAL_SANDBOX_CLIENT_ID=YOUR_SANDBOX_CLIENT_ID_LATER
# PAYPAL_SANDBOX_CLIENT_SECRET=YOUR_SANDBOX_CLIENT_SECRET_LATER
# Public fixture demo. Leave these unset for the default loopback server.
# npm start then binds 127.0.0.1:8787 and ignores HOST and PORT.
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN is the exact https origin opened in the browser.
# The process refuses to start if either PayPal sandbox variable above is set.
# HOST and PORT are the container bind, used only when PUBLIC_ORIGIN is set.
# Example placeholders, not a deployed host:
# PUBLIC_ORIGIN=https://example.com
# HOST=0.0.0.0
# PORT=8787
